  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nHigh pressure settles overhead tonight and will set the stage\nfor what is likely to be the coldest night of the season for\nmost locations. Widespread 20s and some readings down into the\nmid to lower teens in the northern valleys are expected. We are\nalso reaching the tail end of radiation fog season, but a couple\nhours of patchy fog around sunrise remains possible, especially\nsouth of the mtns.\n\nThe next cold front approaches Thu into Fri. Southwest flow will\nallow temps to warm back into the 60s and some 70s. The front\nitself looks to be largely dry again, with some showers most\nlikely for the mtns and points north. Colder air will arrive\nfirst north of the mtns, so Fri may be closer to normal for\nthose locations but still quite warm across the southern\nforecast area.\n\nFor the Halloween weekend high pressure returns with fairly\ntypical late October temps. Then we look toward the start of\nNovember where the pattern looks to become more active again,\nwhich is not saying much after these last couple of weeks.",
